## Part 6: Expected Impact (Revised)

The TASK_689 expected impact table is **optimistic** on agree_hold (85-92%) and **too conservative** on the conditions for success:

| Metric | Current | TASK_689 Expects | My Estimate | Condition |
|--------|---------|-----------------|-------------|-----------|
| agree_hold | 73% | 85-92% | 78-85% | Needs state noise injection |
| agree_trade | 48% | 45-50% | 40-48% | May dip initially |
| balanced_acc | 62% | 65-71% | 63-68% | Conservative first run |
| trade_rate | 27.7% | 5-10% | 10-18% | Heat alone won't suppress 3× |
| over-trading | 7.1× | 1.3-2.5× | 2.5-4.5× | Partial improvement |

**Why more conservative**: The self-correcting heat mechanism relies on out-of-distribution generalization. Without state noise injection during training, the model won't have learned the heat→hold mapping at high heat values. First run will likely show moderate improvement; second run with noise injection should reach the TASK_689 targets.

